      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "SASE X-ray free-electron lasers created a powerful new source for ultrafast structural and matter studies, with consequences across physics and allied sciences.",
        "attribution": "The named researchers made complementary foundational theoretical and practical contributions to the SASE concept and its realization.",
        "maturity": "Operational facilities and a sustained body of science establish both the underlying physics and its importance.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The relative balance between foundational theory, accelerator engineering, and facility-scale realization needs careful expert review."
